---
// Dev-only visual regression page: /dev/styleguide/. Not generated in production builds.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return import.meta.env.DEV ? [{ params: { page: 'styleguide' } }] : [];
}

const swatches = ['bg', 'surface', 'text', 'muted', 'border', 'accent'];
---

<Base title="Style guide">
  <p class="mono-label">Dev only · style guide</p>
  <h1>Heading one, long enough to wrap onto a second line on narrow screens</h1>

  <div class="swatches" role="list">
    {
      swatches.map((name) => (
        <div role="listitem" class="swatch" style={`--c: var(--${name})`}>
          <span class="chip" />
          <span class="mono-label">{name}</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Body text set in Source Serif 4, at a comfortable measure. Here is a{' '}
      <a href="#x">link</a>, some <strong>strong text</strong>, some <em>emphasis</em>, an
      <code>inline_code()</code> span, a <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>K</kbd> shortcut, and some{' '}
      <mark>highlighted</mark> text. Hungarian letters render properly: Laszló, árvíztűrő tükörfúrógép.
      Water is H<sub>2</sub>O, and E = mc<sup>2</sup>.
    </p>

    <h2>Heading two</h2>
    <p>
      The bench does not lie, but it does need calibrating. Ordinary text follows a heading with a
      slightly tighter gap than the gap before it.
    </p>

    <h3>Heading three</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>An unordered item</li>
      <li>
        Another item with a nested list
        <ul>
          <li>Nested one</li>
          <li>Nested two</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <ol>
      <li>First</li>
      <li>Second</li>
    </ol>

    <h4>Heading four</h4>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Because the only thing worse than no data is confidently wrong data.</p>
    </blockquote>

    <pre><code>fn main() &#123;
    println!("hello, bench");
&#125;</code></pre>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Device</th><th>Range</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>HackRF One</td><td>1 MHz – 6 GHz</td><td>Half-duplex, 8-bit ADC, plenty of fun</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RTL-SDR</td><td>24 – 1766 MHz</td><td>Cheap and cheerful, a great first receiver for a long table that needs to scroll</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <figure>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 400 120" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder waveform">
        <rect width="400" height="120" fill="var(--surface)" />
        <path d="M0 60h60l20-45 30 90 30-70 20 25h240" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="3" />
      </svg>
      <figcaption>Figure 1. A placeholder figure with a caption.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <details>
      <summary>A collapsed section</summary>
      <p>Hidden until you open it.</p>
    </details>

    <hr />
    <p>End of the page.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .swatches {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-5);
  }
  .swatch {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }
  .chip {
    width: 5.5rem;
    height: 2.5rem;
    background: var(--c);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
</style>
